{"seqbook":1,"address":"00.00.00"}
{"n":1,"at":"2026-11-09T14:01:37Z","by":"compute","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0000.00","body":"---\ntitle: kernel\ntype: system\nstate: seated\n---"}
{"n":2,"at":"2026-11-09T14:03:14Z","by":"compute","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0012.00","body":"---\ntitle: dictionary\ntype: system\nstate: seated\n---"}
{"n":3,"at":"2026-11-09T14:04:51Z","by":"compute","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0012.03","body":"## seqaddr\ntype: index\ndefault: seqaddr.001\nseqaddr.001: 00.00.00.0050.01.seqaddr\n\n## face\ntype: index\ndefault: face.001\nface.001: 00.00.00.0050.01.face"}
{"n":4,"at":"2026-11-09T14:06:28Z","by":"user","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0020.00","body":"---\ntitle: retry-policy\ntype: system\nstate: seated\n---"}
{"n":5,"at":"2026-11-09T14:08:05Z","by":"claude-opus","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0020.01","body":"## Retry Policy\ntype: rule\naxioms: 1.7.8\n\nA failed write is never retried automatically. Report it and wait."}
{"n":6,"at":"2026-11-09T14:09:42Z","by":"user","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0020.04","body":"## Retry Policy\nsource: [01 / Retry Policy]\nwhy: Retrying hides failures and burns usage.\n\nIf a write fails, the person needs to see it. Silent retries make it look like work went well when it did not. So the kernel says: stop, report, wait for the Director."}
{"n":7,"at":"2026-11-09T14:11:19Z","by":"user","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0021.00","body":"---\ntitle: naming\ntype: system\nstate: seated\n---"}
{"n":8,"at":"2026-11-09T14:12:56Z","by":"claude-opus","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0021.01","body":"## Titles\ntype: rule\n\nTitles are lowercase letters, digits and hyphens. A title is a label, not identity."}
{"n":9,"at":"2026-11-09T14:14:33Z","by":"user","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0021.04","body":"## Titles\nsource: [01 / Titles]\nwhy: Renaming must never break an address.\n\nThe number is the identity. The word after it helps a person read it. Two pages can share a title."}
{"n":10,"at":"2026-11-09T14:16:10Z","by":"user","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0050.00","body":"---\ntitle: faces\ntype: system\nstate: seated\n---"}
{"n":11,"at":"2026-11-09T14:17:47Z","by":"claude-opus","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0050.01","body":"## Seqaddr\ntype: brand\nbrand: seqaddr.001\nforms: seqaddr, seqAddr\nmeans: the sequence address: desk.shelf.book.page.face\n\nAn address reads by position. The page is the anchor.\n\n## Face\ntype: brand\nbrand: face.001\nforms: face, faces\nmeans: one view of a page, for one kind of reader\n\nA page has several faces. Each face is numbered 00 to 08."}
{"n":12,"at":"2026-11-09T14:19:24Z","by":"claude-opus","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0050.02","body":"## Seqaddr\ntype: schema\n\n```\n[DD.][SS.][BB.] PPPP [.FF][.NN] [.title][.tail]\n```"}
{"n":13,"at":"2026-11-09T14:21:01Z","by":"user","op":"put","addr":"00.00.00.0050.04","body":"## Seqaddr\nsource: [01 / Seqaddr], [02 / Seqaddr]\nwhy: One address must find one thing, always.\n\nThe address is the line written down. Each part comes from the one before it, so it stays stable to store.\n\n## Face\nsource: [01 / Face]\nwhy: Different readers need different views of the same page.\n\nA model needs short law. A person needs the long why. The compute needs exact steps. Faces keep them together without mixing them."}
